WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.975
Let me close with what can start now,
because most of it needs no award.

2
00:00:03.975 --> 00:00:06.850
The staff work: write
the application-to-path

3
00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:09.725
routing policy the
controls already ask for.

4
00:00:09.725 --> 00:00:13.650
Its absence is the finding,
not the absence of a device.

5
00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:18.033
Instrument a sample of branches
before the next migration wave,

6
00:00:18.033 --> 00:00:20.762
and verify that DNS really ends at CISA.

7
00:00:20.762 --> 00:00:24.841
Before money moves: send the
target attributes, in writing,

8
00:00:24.841 --> 00:00:27.985
to whoever scopes the
BOD 26-02 replacements,

9
00:00:27.985 --> 00:00:33.424
and ask the field-office request to
separate acquisition from five-year cost.

10
00:00:33.424 --> 00:00:37.725
Before cutover: start CLAW coordination
with CISA and the provider,

11
00:00:37.725 --> 00:00:41.120
have the authorizing official
record the interim gap

12
00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:44.062
as an accepted risk, and
name one decider per row.

13
00:00:44.062 --> 00:00:45.462
One point on urgency.

14
00:00:45.462 --> 00:00:49.317
The branch measurement baseline
can't be reconstructed after

15
00:00:49.317 --> 00:00:52.949
the next migration wave, and it
costs staff time, not capital.

16
00:00:52.949 --> 00:00:56.568
So, the seven decisions: MTIPS
ends on confirmed parity,

17
00:00:56.568 --> 00:01:01.393
the interim gap becomes an accepted
risk, the refresh carries the target,

18
00:01:01.393 --> 00:01:06.217
investment starts with staff time,
the field-office request gets tested,

19
00:01:06.217 --> 00:01:11.363
NPS retirement follows the Entra migration,
and the sequence becomes policy.

20
00:01:11.363 --> 00:01:14.400
Buy transport on physics
and govern it as compliance,

21
00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:17.300
and the branch gets faster
without getting weaker.

22
00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:20.651
Book 09 has the detail,
every claim footnoted,

23
00:01:20.651 --> 00:01:23.550
and the backup slides list the sources.

24
00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:24.380
Thank you.
